@startuml 05-maintenance
title Geonera Ingestion — 5. Maintenance: Auto-Seeder, Gap-Fill & Pruning
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontColor #1B1B1B
skinparam ArrowColor #546E7A
skinparam ArrowFontColor #37474F

skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #FAFAFA
  BorderColor #546E7A
  FontColor #1B1B1B
  FontSize 13

  BackgroundColor<<lock>> #EF6C00
  FontColor<<lock>> #FFFFFF
  BorderColor<<lock>> #A34B00

  BackgroundColor<<db>> #1565C0
  FontColor<<db>> #FFFFFF
  BorderColor<<db>> #0B3C78

  BackgroundColor<<r2>> #2E7D32
  FontColor<<r2>> #FFFFFF
  BorderColor<<r2>> #1B5E20

  BackgroundColor<<api>> #AD1457
  FontColor<<api>> #FFFFFF
  BorderColor<<api>> #6A0F38
}

skinparam activityDiamond {
  BackgroundColor #FFF3CD
  BorderColor #C79100
  FontColor #5D4037
}

skinparam legend {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  BorderColor #90A4AE
  FontColor #1B1B1B
  FontSize 12
  EntrySeparatorColor #CFD8DC
}

skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFFDE7
  BorderColor #C9A227
  FontColor #3E3E3E
}

legend right
  |= Tag |= Meaning |
  |<back:#EF6C00><color:#FFFFFF> lock </color></back>| Advisory-lock / Parent Handler step |
  |<back:#1565C0><color:#FFFFFF> db </color></back>| PostgreSQL transaction (state / outbox) |
  |<back:#2E7D32><color:#FFFFFF> r2 </color></back>| Cloudflare R2 storage I/O |
  |<back:#AD1457><color:#FFFFFF> api </color></back>| External Dukascopy API call |
endlegend

start
:runMaintenanceHandler(ctx, dal);<<lock>>
note right
  Triggered by queue jobs.maintenance
  (ideally every 5 minutes, starting at minute :02).
  Acquires LockIDMaintenance (1003) via Direct Connection.
  Idempotent, batched, and processed strictly per-instrument
  to avoid timeouts, OOM, and long table locks.
end note

split
  ' ============== Forward Seeding ==============
  :**A. Forward Seeding (Batched)**
  Iterate over each Active instrument, per JobType;
  :Find MAX(timestamp) for that
  (instrument_id, job_type) pair
  — the job_type filter is MANDATORY
  to avoid TICK/CANDLE ambiguity;
  :Build a forward chunk of new rows,
  capped at e.g. **30 days (720 hours)**
  per single iteration;
  :Upsert (INSERT ... ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING)
  until the chunk limit or time.Now().UTC()
  is reached;<<db>>
  note right: Remaining days are picked up\nautomatically on the next 5-minute trigger

split again
  ' ============== Historical Sync & Gap Detection ==============
  :**B. Historical Sync & Gap Detection (Batched)**
  Compare MIN(timestamp) WHERE job_type='TICK'
  AND status='CONFIRMED' against
  Instrument.StartDate;

  if (Is MIN(timestamp) NULL?) then (yes — brand-new instrument)
    :Edge case: instrument has never been
    ingested at all. Keep seeding forward
    from StartDate toward "now" gradually,
    **WITHOUT** ever enabling IsPause;
  elseif (MIN(timestamp) > StartDate ?) then (yes — a gap exists)
    :Backward batched insertion — gradually
    Upsert empty rows toward the past
    to close the gap;
    :Run the deterministic check
    **isBackfillComplete(instrumentID, startDate, minConfirmedTime)**:
    1. Compute the Expected Hours Count
       between StartDate and MIN(timestamp)
    2. Count rows in that range that are
       genuinely *stuck*: FAILED, BROKEN,
       ABANDONED, or PROCESSED/PENDING with
       UpdatedAt older than 24h.
       (NOT_FOUND rows still within their
       normal wait cycle — NotFoundStreak < 3 —
       are explicitly EXCLUDED from this count);
    if (Stuck/error rows are blocking MIN from\nregressing toward StartDate?) then (yes — persistent upstream corruption)
      :**Set Instrument.IsPause = true**
      (stop wasting retries on a
      jammed instrument, isolates it
      for engineer review);
    else (no blocking rows found)
      :Gap will continue to close
      naturally over future iterations;
    endif
  else (MIN(timestamp) <= StartDate — already complete)
  endif

  if (Is MIN(timestamp WHERE CONFIRMED) now\nstable and reaching StartDate?) then (yes)
    :**Resume: set Instrument.IsPause = false**;
  endif

split again
  ' ============== Pruning ==============
  :**C. Pruning — Mark & Sweep (2-Phase Commit, Batched)**;
  note right
    DB delete + R2 delete cannot be made atomic
    together — a 2-phase Mark & Sweep avoids
    permanently orphaned objects in storage.
  end note
  :**Phase 1 — Mark (Soft Delete)**
  UPDATE a batch of rows SET IsDeleted = true
  WHERE timestamp < Instrument.StartDate
  AND IsDeleted = false;<<db>>
  note right: Marked rows are immediately\nignored by every ETL worker
  :**Phase 2 — Sweep (Hard Delete)**
  Fetch a batch of rows WHERE IsDeleted = true;
  :For each row, request object deletion
  from Cloudflare R2 first;<<r2>>
  if (R2 responded success or NoSuchKey\n(object already gone)?) then (yes)
    :ONLY THEN issue the physical
    DELETE in PostgreSQL (hard-delete);<<db>>
  else (R2 timeout / error)
    :Leave the row as IsDeleted = true,
    it will be retried automatically
    on the next Pruning cycle (idempotent);
  endif
end split

:wg.Done() x3 — join point
(Parent Handler releases LockIDMaintenance);
stop

@enduml
